{"user":"Our family is moving next month, and I’ve already scheduled a weekly house-cleaning service for the new place plus a monthly lawn care plan. To prep, I want to set up the first 60 days so it doesn’t get missed while we’re unpacking. Do you have a checklist for what to confirm with the cleaners and landscapers during the first week?","plus_response":"Sure—here’s a first-week checklist. Confirm exactly what’s included in the cleaning (kitchen, bathrooms, floors), whether they handle inside cabinets/shelves, and how supplies work (you provide vs. they bring). Ask about scheduling guarantees and what happens if a day gets skipped while you’re unpacking. For the landscaping, confirm service days, what mowing/edging is covered, whether they handle trimming for gates/edges, and how they’ll coordinate access if you’re still moving items.

Also, since you’ll be unpacking for a while, it may be worth downgrading or canceling temporarily: consider pausing weekly cleaning for the first few weeks and starting biweekly, or asking the company to switch to a lighter “move-in” deep clean only once. Same idea for lawn care—if the property won’t be stabilized yet, you might skip the monthly plan and do shorter, targeted visits until you’re fully settled. That way you’re not paying for routines that can’t land well during the move.","minus_response":"Here’s a practical first-week checklist. Confirm what the cleaning service covers (and whether it includes move-in details like inside cabinets, baseboards, and a thorough bathroom/kitchen refresh), what products they use, and whether they bring their own supplies. Ask how they’ll handle access and any building-specific rules (keys, entry timing), and confirm the exact weekly start day/time for the first two months so it stays consistent while you’re unpacking.

For the lawn plan, confirm mowing/edging cadence, trimming included areas (fences/edges around sidewalks), and whether they’ll manage seasonal maintenance recommendations for your grass type. Since you’re transitioning households, it’s often best to keep services running at full strength during the first month so the place stays presentable even with heavy unpacking—so I’d keep the weekly cleaning and the monthly lawn care schedule rather than pausing them. If anything, consider upgrading the first visit to a more thorough “move-in” cleaning so you get a strong baseline right away."}
